message: "If you use this software or its evaluation data, please cite it as below."
title: "Secure containerised architecture for Ollama and Moodle integration: hardened Compose stack, AI provider plugin and red teaming evaluation suite"
type: software
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-06
authors:
  - family-names: "SOB NGHAMI"
    given-names: "Gilles Descartes"
    affiliation: "WINTECHGROUP E-University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4130-5656"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sngdtechnologies/ai-moodle-security"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23891862"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and evaluation artefact accompanying a master's
  thesis on the secure integration of local LLM inference into a Moodle
  learning platform. It contains a hardened Docker Compose stack (seven
  containers, six networks, no outbound route from the application and
  inference containers), a Moodle 4.5 AI subsystem provider plugin
  implementing a four level guardrail pipeline, a seccomp profile and Falco
  runtime rules for the inference container, and a red teaming evaluation
  suite (50 adversarial prompts in five categories, runner, raw results for
  the bare model and the guarded tutor).
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - LLM security
  - container hardening
  - Moodle
  - Ollama
  - Docker
  - data sovereignty
  - red teaming
  - educational technology
